# Criteria section 7 and D90: control for an equation in an unused
# context. Its sides are read as written, each type symbol standing for
# itself, so `T = U` forms although no nesting has T or U in force
# (DeclsForm, AUDIT-CHANGES #74 and #80). All three accept.
type T;
type U;
assume T { fn T.m(); }
context A = T = U, T.m;
fn main() {}
